From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:14:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: google: cpif: ask for a per-CPU receive workqueue
 explicitly

Since the workqueue default changed to unbound, alloc_workqueue() warns
when a caller passes neither WQ_PERCPU nor WQ_UNBOUND, and the warning
with its backtrace was the first thing in every modem bring-up log. The
driver was written for the old per-CPU default: say so.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_device.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_device.c b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_device.c
index a0d8e779e..9a3687777 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_device.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_device.c
@@ -3156,8 +3156,8 @@ static int parse_ect(struct mem_link_device *mld, char *dvfs_domain_name)
 
 static int shmem_rx_setup(struct link_device *ld)
 {
-	ld->rx_wq = alloc_workqueue(
-			"mem_rx_work", WQ_HIGHPRI | WQ_CPU_INTENSIVE, 1);
+	ld->rx_wq = alloc_workqueue("mem_rx_work",
+				    WQ_PERCPU | WQ_HIGHPRI | WQ_CPU_INTENSIVE, 1);
 	if (!ld->rx_wq) {
 		mif_err("%s: ERR! fail to create rx_wq\n", ld->name);
 		return -ENOMEM;
